msgid "Overview of of application research tools for solving differential equations."
msgstr "Pangkalahatang-ideya ng mga application research tool para sa paglutas ng mga differential equation."

# doq: translated after #1094 review 2026-11-21
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Partial differential equations"
msgstr "Mga partial differential equation"

# doq: translated after #1094 review 2026-11-21
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Partial differential equations {#partial-differential-equations}"
msgstr "Mga partial differential equation {#partial-differential-equations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This active area of research explores how quantum algorithms can help solve partial differential equations that describe physical systems and processes, such as fluid dynamics, heat transfer, electromagnetic fields, and quantum mechanical systems. Approaches include quantum algorithms for linear systems of equations, which can be applied to certain discretized differential equations, as well as quantum methods for differential equations that directly exploit quantum circuits or quantum state representations. These techniques can offer computational advantages for specific large-scale problems, particularly when the solution can be efficiently encoded in and extracted from a quantum state. However, their practical benefits depend on factors such as problem structure, data encoding, hardware requirements, and the cost of retrieving the solution.\n"
msgstr "Tinutuklas ng aktibong larangang ito ng pananaliksik kung paano makakatulong ang mga quantum algorithm sa paglutas ng mga partial differential equation na naglalarawan ng mga pisikal na sistema at proseso, tulad ng fluid dynamics, heat transfer, electromagnetic field, at mga quantum mechanical na sistema. Kasama sa mga approach ang mga quantum algorithm para sa mga linear system ng equation, na maaaring ilapat sa ilang discretized na differential equation, pati ang mga quantum method para sa mga differential equation na direktang gumagamit ng mga quantum circuit o representasyon ng quantum state. Maaaring magbigay ang mga teknik na ito ng computational advantage para sa mga partikular na malakihang problema, lalo na kapag mahusay na maie-encode ang solusyon sa isang quantum state at makukuha mula rito. Gayunpaman, ang praktikal na benepisyo ng mga ito ay nakadepende sa mga salik tulad ng estruktura ng problema, data encoding, mga kinakailangan sa hardware, at gastos ng pagkuha ng solusyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A common workflow encodes a trial solution as a parameterized quantum circuit, then classically optimizes the circuit parameters so that the resulting quantum state approximates the true solution of the differential equation across a set of sample points. This variational approach can accommodate boundary and initial conditions, and can be combined with multiple classical optimizers in sequence to improve convergence. The application function on this page automates this workflow for specific domains, so that you can supply physical parameters and boundary conditions directly, without implementing the underlying encoding and optimization loop yourself.\n"
msgstr "Ang karaniwang workflow ay nag-e-encode ng trial na solusyon bilang parameterized na quantum circuit, at pagkatapos ay classical na ino-optimize ang mga parameter ng circuit para ang nagreresultang quantum state ay tumantiya sa totoong solusyon ng differential equation sa isang set ng mga sample point. Kayang tanggapin ng variational approach na ito ang mga boundary at initial condition, at maaaring pagsamahin sa maraming classical optimizer nang sunud-sunod para pahusayin ang convergence. Ino-automate ng application function sa pahinang ito ang workflow na ito para sa mga partikular na domain, para direkta mong maibigay ang mga pisikal na parameter at boundary condition, nang hindi ka mismo nagpapatupad ng pinagbabatayang encoding at optimization loop.\n"

